-- Link — a typed navigable link: a URL + an optional label. forms-collapse
-- Phase 5 (R2 — the funnel returns a typed value). A funnel function returns a
-- `Link` as its "next screen"; the embeddable `FenelForm` widget renders it as a
-- "Continue →" anchor the visitor clicks (render a value's VIEW, not obey a
-- directive — LOCK-1). This replaces the R1 `funnelRedirect`/`funnelPage`
-- compat-shim records (deleted in Phase 5): a redirect is now a real typed
-- value, not a `{redirect = url}` directive the widget special-cases.
--
-- Reuses the `UrlStr` refined-String atom from proxy_link.fenel (String |
-- value ∈ format:url) rather than minting a new url refinement — UrlStr is
-- already a cross-entity atom (proxy_link + page both bind it). References
-- resolve by name in the shared `entities` registry at lookup time, so Link
-- referencing UrlStr is fine as long as proxy_link.fenel is also loaded (it is).
--
-- Single-ctor named-field record (head == ctor, like proxy_link's ProxyLink) —
-- it lowers to a `$record`, but a constructed `Link { … }` value still carries
-- `$tag: "Link"` (the construct op tags by ctor name regardless of the type's
-- $record/$variant shape), which is what the widget reads to recognise it.
--
-- `label` (Maybe String) earns its slot: it lets a funnel override the anchor
-- text ("Continue →" is the default when Nothing). Identity (label / description
-- / icon) is authored as facet directives — NOT a TS defineSystemEntity literal
-- (no language concept in TS).

@entity
@codeName "Link"
@label "Link"
@description "A navigable link — a URL plus an optional anchor label"
@icon "link"
Link = Link url: UrlStr label: Maybe String
